// A word that is not an item keyword. NEITHER compiler parses `static`, so the
// port's old answer - "this item kind not yet ported" - claimed a gap between them
// that this input does not show; the reference answers by LISTING what it accepts,
// and the two only agree once the port says the same thing.
//
// This fixture used to live in tests/fuzzlimits, where it pinned that the fuzzer
// RECOGNISED the port's announced border from that exact wording. Its own comment
// named the exit it has now taken: once the port stops announcing a border, the
// limit is retired and the entry re-measured rather than left to outlive its
// subject. What remains measurable is parity, which is what this corpus compares.
static X: int = 1;
fn main() { println(1); }
